 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Thresholds Support
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` parameter: an object mapping metric IDs to minimum scores (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }`).
+- When thresholds are provided, the report includes:
+  - `passed` (boolean): true if all thresholds are met, false otherwise.
+  - `thresholds` (array): one entry per threshold with `{ metric, min, score, passed }`.
+  - A metric with `score: null` fails its threshold (instead of crashing or passing).
+- CLI: `--threshold <metric>=<min>` can be specified multiple times.
+  - Exit 0 if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds).
+  - Exit 1 if any threshold fails.
+  - Exit 2 if thresholds are malformed or metric id is unknown.
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL for each.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
